@startuml class-resolution
title Resolution — a typestate, not a runtime flag

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "proc_macro_flow_traits::resolution" <<Frame>> {

  class "Unresolved<'ast, T>" as Unresolved {
    -tokens: &'ast TokenStream
    -_target: PhantomData<fn() -> T>
    --
    +new(&'ast TokenStream) -> Self
    +resolve() -> Result<Resolved<'ast,T>, Error>
    +resolve_with<E>(f) -> Result<Resolved<'ast,T>, E>
  }

  class "Resolved<'ast, T>" as Resolved {
    -value: T
    -tokens: &'ast TokenStream
    --
    +value() -> &T
    +into_value() -> T
  }
  note right of Resolved
    **No ""resolve"" method.**
    Resolving twice is a type error, not a
    silent no-op — the idempotence problem
    disappears rather than being handled.
    (#no-idempotence)
  end note

  interface "Deferred<'ast>" as Deferred {
    +tokens() -> &'ast TokenStream
  }
  note bottom of Deferred
    Bounds ""Stage::Item"". Without it, code
    generic over a stage would hold an item
    it could not touch.
  end note

  interface Stage {
    +type Item<'ast, T>: Deferred + ToTokens
  }
  note right of Stage
    STAGE-level, not item-level: a container
    takes ONE parameter however many deferred
    fields it has, and transitions wholesale.
    A container cannot hold a mix — "half
    parsed" is not a state anything downstream
    should have to consider.
  end note

  class Raw <<uninhabited enum>>
  class Parsed <<uninhabited enum>>
}

Unresolved ..> Resolved : resolve()\n**consumes self**
Unresolved ..|> Deferred
Resolved ..|> Deferred
Raw ..|> Stage
Parsed ..|> Stage
Raw ..> Unresolved : Item
Parsed ..> Resolved : Item

note as Splice
  Both states implement ""ToTokens"" and emit
  the SAME tokens. A generator never has to
  ask which state it is holding — splicing
  is uniform, and resolution never costs you
  the source.
end note

Splice .. Unresolved
Splice .. Resolved

note as Contrast
  **Why a typestate here but not for Extraction**

  Resolved/unresolved is a true binary with no
  second axis. Extraction has one — a node can
  have a value AND a complaint — so it is a
  struct. The two decisions are consistent,
  not a reversal.
end note

Contrast .. Stage

@enduml
